---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Status And Limits | DP-LMI Package">
  <section class="hero compact">
    <h1>Status And Limits</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The current public surface is intentionally narrow: direct
      coefficient-wise YALMIP assembly over cell-local Bernstein data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Implemented Now</h2>
    <table class="status-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Area</th>
          <th>Current behavior</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dpmat</code></td>
          <td>Known-data construction, evaluation, display, plotting, structural operations, coefficient algebra, matrix products, and zero simplifications.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dpvar</code></td>
          <td>YALMIP-backed affine decision expressions, supported known-data products, matrix operations, comparisons, and rate derivatives.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dplmi</code></td>
          <td>Direct finite coefficient-wise constraints, rate-row enumeration, <code>toYalmip</code>, and solver smoke tests.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Documentation</td>
          <td>LaTeX manual in <code>doc/manual.tex</code> and GitHub Pages source in <code>webpage/</code>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Reserved Future Work</h2>
    <p>
      Relaxation lemma assembly, Polya relaxation, strictness margins,
      residual diagnostics, and package-owned solver wrappers are not
      documented as implemented APIs. Users currently call YALMIP directly
      after converting <code>dplmi</code> objects with <code>toYalmip</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
